room.g2.en:
I was daydreaming and     
couldn't focus in class;
my fault, but still a shock...

From now on,  
keep working on yourself; 
don't forget it.

Babysitting isn't     
just keeping kids happy;
it takes more than that.

Oh, don't mention it.   
You're from a famous school;    
this much is only natural.

Times are changing. 
Yes, not only the sword now;  
magic's age dawns...

Gloom weighs on the people  
and laughter fades from town; 
now is when hearts need art.

Somehow you can't leave him be; 
he makes you want to coddle him.
Hee hee!

Of course,
if the tips come flying,
all the better. Heh heh heh!

Today I leave the kids I  
raised so devotedly;    
it still hurts...

if you can't see that,
no business 
will ever do well.

Especially magical goods; 
many of them you can only   
get here, I think.

My readings never miss; 
whatever it is, I'll  
hit it dead on.

(Somehow, I feel the
Bishop will be with us
for ages yet...)

Going into politics,
if you hit a wall,  
remember this.

Long, long ago.   
Magic did not yet matter;   
wars were fought by arms.

Flattening a mountain,  
one blow through a wall;  
even half of it is amazing.

Not weapons or armor, though;   
all she ever buys are 
tonics and potions.

Fear not. I would not devour  
a guest come from so far;     
I swear it on my name.

Milady would enjoy the  
paintings and odd sculptures;   
she will not be bored.

Indeed it is so.  
The weather is fine today;
perhaps tea at my manor...

There are so many people today; 
is the Prince 
here too, I wonder?

She is your daughter, after all;
taking up the sword 
would suit her.

The nobles' era is over;
now it's the merchants'!  
Is that true...?

Think it over. Forget being a 
high-born but dull noblewoman;
a far more exciting life awaits.

Seeing you in danger        
from demons... um,
I hate it.

The nobles' era is over;
now it's the merchants'!  
Is that true...?

It holds great magic; 
one punch with it can even  
shatter rock.

Kreis: magic stone profit;
the Minister: the 
kingdom's growth. A match.

Milady, a fine effort.  
You were but one step away; 
such a pity.

Cube, you're a demon yourself;
you must know one or two, 
right?

Ruling Dark Town isn't enough 
for me. I'll take the market, 
and downtown too. All mine!

A super fancy carriage
is parked outside;
they want you, Sir!
